  "answer": "Double circulation is a system in which blood passes through the heart twice during one complete cycle. In humans, it is important because it ensures that blood is efficiently circulated to all parts of the body and also to the lungs for oxygenation. The process involves two separate cycles: pulmonary circulation, where blood is sent to the lungs to pick up oxygen and return to the heart, and systemic circulation, where blood is pumped to the rest of the body and returns to the heart. This system allows for efficient oxygen and nutrient delivery while removing waste products.",
